I don't have much solid information, but I did want to mention that I was=
=20
able to boot an AlphaStation 500/500 via bootp last summer (August 2001). =
=20
This was with the then-current woody installer, then called testing.

I did not use serial console, so it's possible that's what's fouling you=20
up.    I see you downloaded alpha.img rather than building it yourself. =20
Are you sure the kernel within contains support for serial console?  Can=20
you hook up a monitor for the install process?  Just about any=20
same-vintage PCI graphics card should be sufficient for just a text=20
console display.

I used dhcpd, not bootp, for this process.  Much easier to configure. =20
Here's the dhcpd.conf entry I used for this system:

host bret {
	hardware ethernet 0:0:f8:24:e4:1e;
	filename "tftpboot.img";
	fixed-address 192.168.1.125;
	server-name "jekyl.doug.ties.org";
}

You should also make sure you have the latest console firmware.  The good=
=20
news is you can flash the firmware over tftp/bootp!  Very cool!  If you're=
=20
unable to find it, I think I have the proper file lying around -- contact=
=20
me offlist.

Good luck!
-Doug



