Welcome to travel in China, welcome to Beijing!

Hi! It's nice to meet you on Internet. I'm not sure whether you have tours to China or not. But I'd like to cooperate with you in travel business.
We Beijing Cultural Relics International Travel Service Co. Ltd. is one of the leading travel agencies in China. We provide best service to travelers. All the tourist guides of our company are well-trained and most experienced. The following is one of our highly recommended Beijing tour schedules.

Route 1
Beijing/Xian/Shanghai/Suzhou--10nights 11days

Day 1: Beijing
Arrive in Beijing. Where you will be met by your local guide. Transfer to your hotel. Remainder of day at leisure. 

Day 2: Beijing                           (B-breakfast, L-lunch, D-dinner)
Full day tour to the Tian'anmen Square, the largest square in the world, then the Forbidden City, where 24 emperors lived and ruled China. After lunch, visit the Temple of Heaven, which is considered one of the finest buildings ever constructed in ancient China. Today we'll have our special dinner in the Dai Village restaurant with singing and dancing show. (Dai minority people are the origin of Thailand people.) 

Day 3: Beijing                          (B L D)
Today will be one of the highlights of the trip as you visit and climb the Great Wall of China and the Ming Tombs along the Sacred Way with lunch and special dinner. Today's special dinner is Sichuan cuisine, which concentrates on spicy food.

Day 4: Beijing                         (B L D)
Today you will have a wonderful and special tour - People's Commune (including visit to primary school, farmers' houses, Home for the aged, Greenhouses, the orchard, big local market, etc.). Visit a Middle School not far from the commune. Lunch in the farmers' houses or in the town hall of the commune. Afternoon tour to the Summer Palace, the Imperial Garden. Today's special dinner is Xinjiang Uyghur food. (It is one minority in northwest of China, which is the starting point of Ancient Silk Road)

Day 5: Beijing                        (B L D)
Have a visit to Beijing Opera School, Where you can communicate with the students of the school and see how they have their special training. After lunch,  visit the famous Lama Temple and Beijing Zoo where you can see the lovely Giant Pandas. Hotpot and Barbecue dinner and Peking Opera in the evening.

Day 6: Beijing                        (B D)
This is a day to explore on your own. It will be your final day for shopping and sightseeing in Beijing.
Suggestion: Wangfujing Street, Silk Alley, etc. 
Peking Roast Duck dinner.

Day 7: Beijing/Xian                           (B D)
Morning flight to Xian. Lunch on board. Meet your guide upon arrival and transferred to your hotel. After lunch, afternoon tour to the Shaanxi Provincial Museum, one of the best museums in China. Then stroll on the ancient City Wall. Today's special dinner is Chinese meal with local flavor, special noodles are been made right in front of you by the local chef.

Day 8: Xian                            (B L D)
Full day tour to the Big Wild Goose Pagoda, which was built in 652 in the Tang Dynasty to safekeep the 657 volumes of Buddhist scriptures brought back from India by Monk Xuan Zang. The highlight in the afternoon is the Terra-Cotta Warriors and Horses Museum-the eighth wonder of the world. You will visit thousands of life-size Terra-cotta warriors and horses guarding the Tomb of the first emperor of China, Qin Shi Huang (221-210BC). With lunch and special dumpling dinner.

Day 9: Xian/Shanghai               (B L D)
Morning flight to Shanghai. Shanghai, the "Paradise of Adventurers" in the past and China's commercial center today, is the most sophisticated city in China. After lunch visit Shanghai Art Museum. Then taste the Shanghai local food. At night, stroll along Nanjing Road, the busiest shopping center of Shanghai. 

Day 10: Shanghai/Suzhou/Shanghai       (B L D)
A full-day excursion to Suzhou by coach. Suzhou is known as "Venice in the East" and famous for its silk industry as well. There you will visit the Humble Administrator's Garden, Garden of Master Fishnet (World Heritage Site listed by UNESCO) and the silk factory. With lunch and dinner. Then back to Shanghai.

Day 11: Shanghai                    (B L)
Morning tour to Yu Garden and Jade Buddha Temple. After lunch transfer to airport and departure.


Fee: USD748$/p (for group above 10 pax)
Tour prices include: Three hotel accommodations (on twin sharing basis), all meals as listed, air-conditioned tour bus, admission fares, travel insurance in China; air fare for all domestic flights (Beijing to Xian, Xian to Shanghai) with domestic airport taxes, and local transportation and transfers within China, well trained English speaking tour guides. 
 
Tour prices do not include: Transportation from your country to and back from China; airport departure tax for international flight (90yuan/p), customs fee; China Visa fee; optional tours/meals. Gratitude to guide and driver is not included.

